;; Knoxx-owned translation pipeline configuration.
;;
;; This replaces the legacy `/v1/translations/config` endpoint as the authority
;; for translation model and review policy. Both the review UI and the JVM
;; ingestion worker resolve from this resource through
;; `/api/translations/config`, so neither can reinterpret model precedence for
;; itself.
;;
;; `:translation/model` is a catalog model id spelled exactly as
;; `contracts/models/*.edn` spells it — a plain string, because real ids contain
;; `/`, `:` and `.` and are not keyword-safe. It is validated against the model
;; catalog on every read and write; an id absent from the catalog fails before a
;; worker attempts a translation.
;;
;; Per-org overrides live in a manifest namespaced `orgs.<org-id>` with
;; `:policy/id :translation-pipeline`, and merge onto this default before
;; catalog validation.
{:namespace :knoxx.translation
 :resources
 [{:policy/id :pipeline-default
   :contract/doc "Authoritative translation pipeline configuration for Knoxx."
   :translation/model "glm-5"
   :translation/source-locale :en
   :translation/default-review :required}]}
